          "alternative": "The existing memory, routing, pooling, or consolidation machinery may explain the gains over the mixture; correction may be negligible or harmful, and the guard may rarely change it enough to affect predictions.",
          "expected_evidence": "A reproducible positive paired guarded-minus-unguarded effect near switches, with no material stable or frozen-recall loss, would support a useful guard; a confidence interval excluding a prespecified 1 percentage point benefit would weigh against it. If no-correction wins, correction itself may be harmful. Guard values near one or tiny applied corrections would suggest insufficient activation; substantial activation without accuracy gains would suggest the guard lacks useful effect.",
